.TH BOOTSTASH 5 "September 2026" "bootstash" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
bootstash \- operator config, dist defaults, and OIDC secrets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/default/bootstash
.br
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist
.br
.I /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
bootstashd reads dist defaults
.RI ( /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist ;
packaged operator keys, including empty/derived; not OIDC),
then
.IR /etc/default/bootstash ,
then
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json .
Later source wins for scalars. If the operator file mentions
.B LISTEN
at all, its
.B LISTEN=
lines replace the packaged listen list (several
.B LISTEN=
lines in
.I /etc/default/bootstash
append to each other). The secrets file cannot change
.BR LISTEN .
.PP
.I /etc/default/bootstash
is not a conffile.
Configure creates it from
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default
if the path is missing (commented
.BR DATA ,
.BR LISTEN ,
.BR PUBLIC_URL ,
and
.BR ADMIN_USERS ).
.B dpkg
does not prompt to merge a new packaged copy over operator edits.
Add only keys that differ from
.IR /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist .
Do not copy the full dist file into
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
.B bootstash provision-google
does not write this file.
If the operator deletes this file,
configure copies
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default
back if the path is missing. It does not enable the unit.
If the daemon is already running it
.BR try-restart s
after cert sync (copy, or dest PEM removal when
.BR TLS=no );
if it is down it starts only when
.B bootstash check-config
would pass (same as
.BR bootstashd \-t ).
First install without a Google client id stays down.
It prints remaining steps (daemon not started or not enabled on
boot, no Google client id, loopback
.BR LISTEN ,
no copied certs unless
.BR TLS=no ).
.PP
.I /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json
is the Google Web application client JSON
.B bootstash provision-google
installs. It is not a conffile. Do not put
.BR LISTEN ,
.BR PUBLIC_URL ,
or other operator keys there.
.PP
Format:
.B KEY=value
lines,
.B #
comments, no shell expansion.
.I /etc/default/bootstash
and
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist
are
.BR 0644
.BR root:root
(same as other
.I /etc/default
files).
.I /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json
is
.BR 0640
.BR root:bootstash .
The daemon reads these files itself; do not use systemd
.BR EnvironmentFile= .
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B PUBLIC_URL
Browser-facing URL (scheme and host, no trailing slash).
Used for OIDC redirects, cookies, CSRF Origin checks, and the
origin a road warrior pastes into OpenVPN Connect (not a file
path).
.B X-Forwarded-Proto
and
.B X-Forwarded-Host
are ignored.
When unset, the daemon uses
.B CERT_NAME
(or
.B hostname \-f
if none) and the first TCP
.B LISTEN
port, with scheme
.B https
when cert files are present
.RB ( TLS=auto ).
.B TLS=no
forces
.BR http .
Ports 80 and 443 are omitted.
.B localhost
is not used.
Write this when the browser’s URL is not that host.
HTTPS session cookies are host-only.
Extra DNS names must
.B Redirect
here; do not proxy the same backend on two names.
See
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/OPENVPN.md
(Origin models) and
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/examples .
.TP
.B LISTEN
Repeatable listen spec:
.IR where:port
with optional
.B /ipv4
or
.BR /ipv6 .
.I where
may be
.BR * ,
an address, a CIDR, an interface name, or
.BR unix://path .
Port 0 is rejected. Unix sockets are HTTP only.
A CIDR is expanded to
.B local
addresses in that prefix, not a client allowlist.
Loopback is skipped unless the prefix is loopback.
If no address matches at start, the daemon refuses to run; on reload
it keeps the previous listeners.
A missing interface is retried at start and kept on reload.
.TP
.B TLS
Default
.B auto
(also
.BR maybe ):
HTTPS when a cert pair is found, otherwise HTTP.
.B yes
.RB / true / on / 1
are the same as
.BR auto .
.B no
forces HTTP on TCP binds.
The Let’s Encrypt hook does not copy
.I live/
into
.I /etc/bootstash/certs
and removes dest PEMs there so
.B bootstash
does not hold an unused private key.
.I live/
is untouched.
.B TLS_CERT
/
.B TLS_KEY
are also ignored.
.BR false / 0 / off
are the same as
.BR no .
Other values are an error.
An explicit
.B PUBLIC_URL
keeps its scheme (a proxy may terminate TLS).
Derived
.B PUBLIC_URL
is
.B http
when
.BR TLS=no .
.TP
.B OVPN_TOKEN
Default
.B auto
(same synonyms as
.BR TLS ).
Mint Connect URL-import tokens and send
.B Ovpn-WebAuth
on the probe.
.B no
turns that off for the whole site (reload).
A user can also drop
.B .bootstash-no-ovpn-token
in their cubby root.
See
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/OPENVPN.md .
.TP
.B TLS_CERT / TLS_KEY
If both are set, TCP binds use HTTPS with these files unless
.BR TLS=no .
When unset, the daemon uses
.I /etc/bootstash/certs/<name>/fullchain.pem
and
.I privkey.pem
if both exist.
.I name
is
.BR CERT_NAME
(see below).
Do not point these at
.IR /etc/letsencrypt/live
.RB ( User=bootstash
cannot read it).
.TP
.B CERT_NAME
Let’s Encrypt lineage / directory under
.IR /etc/bootstash/certs .
When unset, the hook (which can read
.IR live/ )
chooses the
.B PUBLIC_URL
host,
.BR live/ $(hostname -f),
or the only
.I live/
lineage; the daemon then sees that
.I certs/<name>/
pair.
.B TLS=no
skips that copy and removes dest PEMs.
Several lineages and no chosen name
.RB ( CERT_NAME ,
.B PUBLIC_URL
host, or
.BR hostname \-f
match):
.B sync
prints the list and copies nothing.
A name already in
.I certs/
is still refreshed on renew when no name is chosen.
The hook does not rewrite the operator file; the daemon
derives
.B CERT_NAME
and
.B PUBLIC_URL
at runtime.
Not an ACME client.
.TP
.B DATA
Data volume. Default
.IR /var/lib/bootstash
.RB ( 0751
so a cubby owner can traverse in).
.I users/
is
.B 0711
so a linked Unix user can
.B bootstash put
or copy into
.IR users/<name>/
.RB ( 2770
.IR name:bootstash )
without listing other cubbies.
Start, SIGHUP, and
.B /home
GET/HEAD set cubby files to group
.B bootstash
and
.BR 0640 .
See
.BR bootstashd (8).
.TP
.B OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
Google web OAuth client. Client ID is required to start.
Do not put these in
.I /etc/default/bootstash
or
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist
(those files are
.BR 0644 ).
They come from
.I /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json
(the JSON the Google console downloads:
.B web.client_id
/
.BR web.client_secret ).
.B bootstash provision-google
installs that file
.RB ( 0640
.BR root:bootstash ).
A KEY=value secrets file is still read.
.TP
.B OIDC_CRYPTO
Optional HMAC key (at least 32 bytes, or hex). Do not put this in
.I /etc/default/bootstash
or
.IR /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist .
If unset, a key is created under
.IR $DATA/state/crypto.key .
.TP
.B PAM_SERVICE
PAM service name. Default
.BR bootstashd
(file
.IR /etc/pam.d/bootstashd ).
.B bootstashd
does not call PAM as
.BR bootstash :
it execs
.IR /usr/lib/bootstash/pam
(setuid root). The
.B bootstash
CLI does not use PAM.
.TP
.B MAX_UPLOAD
Upload size cap in bytes (suffixes such as
.B 32MiB
are accepted). Default 32MiB.
.TP
.B UNIX_GROUP
Group for Unix sockets. Default
.BR bootstash .
.TP
.B ADMIN_USERS
Comma- or space-separated PAM usernames treated as operators (the
admin seam). Default empty: nobody. SIGHUP re-reads the list.
Currently grants no extra HTTP powers. Listing or dropping a PAM
link is
.B bootstash links
/
.B bootstash unlink
(access to
.IR $DATA/state ),
not this list. Later admin HTTP routes will use this list.
Not a Unix group and not an application user table.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/bootstash
Operator overrides
.RB ( 0644
.BR root:root ).
Not a conffile; created from
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default
if missing.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default
Operator-file template (not a conffile).
.TP
.I /etc/bootstash
Directory for helper-written secrets and copied TLS files
.RB ( 0750
.BR root:bootstash ).
Created by tmpfiles or the helper. Do not use systemd
.BR ConfigurationDirectory= .
.TP
.I /etc/bootstash/certs/<name>
.I fullchain.pem
and
.I privkey.pem
readable by
.BR bootstash
.RB ( 0640
.BR root:bootstash ).
Filled by
.IR /usr/lib/bootstash/letsencrypt-deploy
(linked from
.IR /etc/letsencrypt/renewal-hooks/deploy/bootstash ).
Certbot runs that hook on issue and renew for the
chosen lineage. The package runs
.B letsencrypt-deploy sync
on configure (prints if nothing matches).
.B TLS=no
skips the copy and removes dest PEMs.
See
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/QUICKSTART.md .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bootstashd (8),
.BR bootstash (8),
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/OPENVPN.md
